{"name":"Here Comes the Sun","hex":"#fcdf63","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"here","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In, on, or at this place (a place perceived to be close to the speaker); compare there.","At this point or stage (in a process, argument, narration, etc.)"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alive"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/here"},{"term":"comes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of come"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The answer to the theme, or dux, in a fugue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/comes"},{"term":"sun","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Sundanese."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The star that is closest to the Earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun"}],"entries":[{"title":"Here Comes the Sun","blocks":[{"text":"\"Here Comes the Sun\" is a song by the English rock band the Beatles from their eleventh studio album Abbey Road (1969). It was written and sung by George Harrison, and is one of his best-known compositions. Harrison wrote the song in April 1969 at the country house of his friend Eric Clapton, where Harrison had chosen to play truant for the day to avoid attending a meeting at the Beatles' Apple Corps organisation. The lyrics reflect his relief at the arrival of spring and the temporary respite he was experiencing from the band's business affairs."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/41/Thebeatles_here_comes_the_sun.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Here_Comes_the_Sun","wikidata":"Q210401"},{"title":"Here Comes the Sun (Dennis-Benn novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Here Comes the Sun is a 2016 novel by Nicole Dennis-Benn set in Montego Bay, Jamaica and published by Liveright Publishing Corporation. Dennis-Benn's debut novel, the book examines social issues in Jamaica, including skin bleaching, sex work, homophobia, rape, and the impact of tourism on local residents. The novel won the Lambda Literary Award for Lesbian Fiction."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d3/Here_Comes_the_Sun_%28Nicole_Dennis-Benn%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Here_Comes_the_Sun_(Dennis-Benn_novel)","wikidata":"Q110661200"},{"title":"Here Comes","blocks":[{"text":"Here Comes EP is an EP from the album Up from Below by Edward Sharpe and the Magnetic Zeros. It was released in May 2009."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/Hearcomesepcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Here_Comes","wikidata":"Q5737069"},{"title":"Comes","blocks":[{"text":"Comes, translated as count, was a Roman title, generally linked to a comitatus or comital office."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comes","wikidata":"Q1071047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Ewhurst_mill.jpg/330px-Ewhurst_mill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Ewhurst_mill.jpg/330px-Ewhurst_mill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hurt Wood windmill in Ewhurst, Surrey. Harrison wrote \"Here Comes the Sun\" in the garden at nearby Hurtwood Edge.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEwhurst_mill.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Moog_Synthesizer_3P_%281972%29%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg/500px-Moog_Synthesizer_3P_%281972%29%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Moog_Synthesizer_3P_%281972%29%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg/1280px-Moog_Synthesizer_3P_%281972%29%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Moog_Synthesizer_3P_%281972%29%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg/500px-Moog_Synthesizer_3P_%281972%29%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An early 1970s version of the Moog 3-series synthesiser used on the song","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoog_Synthesizer_3P_(1972)%2C_CRuNCh_Lab.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Richie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg/500px-Richie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Richie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg/1280px-Richie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Richie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg/500px-Richie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Richie Havens had the biggest hit of his career with the song.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARichie_Havens_1972_Hamburg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Steve_Harley_%26_Cockney_Rebel_Here_Comes_the_Sun_1976_Single.jpg/250px-Steve_Harley_%26_Cockney_Rebel_Here_Comes_the_Sun_1976_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Steve_Harley_%26_Cockney_Rebel_Here_Comes_the_Sun_1976_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/58/Steve_Harley_%26_Cockney_Rebel_Here_Comes_the_Sun_1976_Single.jpg/250px-Steve_Harley_%26_Cockney_Rebel_Here_Comes_the_Sun_1976_Single.jpg?utm_source=e